<title>USA: Monarch Bancorp completes reverse split, merger.</title>
<headline>Monarch Bancorp completes reverse split, merger.</headline>
<dateline>LAGUNA NIGUEL, Calif. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monarch Bancorp said that shareholders have approved its merger with California Commercial Bankshares, a reverse stock split and a name change.</p>
<p>Monarch, which is now to be called Western Bancorp, said its acquisition of California Commercial was completed on June 4. It has begun trading on the Nasdaq under the symbol, WEBC.</p>
<p>Related to the deal, the company set a 1-for-8.5 reverse stock split.</p>
<p>The total value of the deal was not disclosed.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
